{"id":"mahabharata-7-099","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":99,"title":"नवनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 99 · Satyaki beats Duhshasana","summary":{"en":"Duhshasana attacks Satyaki with thousands of arrows and a terrible spear, which Satyaki cuts to pieces. Satyaki defeats him and goes on toward where Arjuna fights.","kn":"ದುಃಶಾಸನ ಸಾವಿರಾರು ಬಾಣ ಮತ್ತು ಭೀಕರ ಶಕ್ತಿಯಿಂದ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಅದನ್ನು ತುಂಡರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸಿ ಅರ್ಜುನ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಿರುವತ್ತ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुःशासन हज़ारों बाणों और भयंकर शक्ति से सात्यकि पर आक्रमण करता है, जिसे सात्यकि टुकड़े कर देता है। वह उसे हराकर वहाँ आगे बढ़ता है जहाँ अर्जुन लड़ रहे हैं।","te":"దుశ్శాసనుడు వేల బాణాలతో, భయంకర శక్తితో సాత్యకిపై దాడి చేస్తాడు; సాత్యకి దాన్ని ముక్కలు చేస్తాడు. అతన్ని ఓడించి అర్జునుడు పోరాడుతున్న చోటికి సాగుతాడు.","ta":"துச்சாசனன் ஆயிரக்கணக்கான அம்புகளோடும் கொடிய வேலோடும் சாத்யகியைத் தாக்க, சாத்யகி அதைத் துண்டாக்குகிறான். அவனை வென்று அர்ஜுனன் போரிடும் இடம் நோக்கி முன்னேறுகிறான்.","ml":"ദുശ്ശാസനൻ സാത്യകിയെ ആയിരക്കണക്കിന് അമ്പുകളും ഭയങ്കരമായ കുന്തവുംകൊണ്ട് ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; സാത്യകി അത് കഷണങ്ങളാക്കുന്നു. ദുശ്ശാസനനെ തോൽപ്പിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം അർജുനൻ പോരാടുന്നിടത്തേക്ക് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.99; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो दुःशासनो राजञ्शैनेयं समुपाद्रवत् ।\nकिरञ्शरसहस्राणि पर्जन्य इव वृष्टिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duhshasana, O king, rushed at Shaineya, scattering thousands of arrows like a rain-giving cloud."}},{"n":2,"text":"स विद्ध्वा सात्यकिं षष्ट्या तथा षोडशभिः शरैः ।\nनाकम्पयत्स्थितं युद्धे मैनाकमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having struck Satyaki with sixty and sixteen arrows, he could not shake him as he stood in the battle, like the Mainaka mountain."}},{"n":3,"text":"स तु दुःशासनं वीरः सायकैरावृणोद्भृशम् ।\nमशकं समनुप्राप्तमूर्णनाभिरिवोर्णया ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the hero covered Duhshasana heavily with arrows, as a spider covers a gnat that has come near with its thread."}},{"n":4,"text":"दृष्ट्वा दुःशासनं राजा तथा शरशताचितम् ।\nत्रिगर्तांश्चोदयामास युयुधानरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Duhshasana buried under hundreds of arrows, the king urged the Trigartas on toward Yuyudhana's chariot."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेऽगच्छन्युयुधानस्य समीपं क्रूरकारिणः ।\nत्रिगर्तानां त्रिसाहस्रा रथा युद्धविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three thousand cruel Trigarta chariots, skilled in battle, came near Yuyudhana."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते तु तं रथवंशेन महता पर्यवारयन् ।\nस्थिरां कृत्वा मतिं युद्धे भूत्वा संशप्तका मिथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They surrounded him with a great line of chariots, firmly resolving on battle and pledging themselves among themselves as Samshaptakas."}},{"n":7,"text":"तेषां प्रयततां युद्धे शरवर्षाणि मुञ्चताम् ।\nयोधान्पञ्चशतान्मुख्यानग्रानीके व्यपोथयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they struggled and showered arrows in the battle, he struck down five hundred chief warriors at the head of the force."}},{"n":8,"text":"तेऽपतन्त हतास्तूर्णं शिनिप्रवरसायकैः ।\nमहामारुतवेगेन रुग्णा इव महाद्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down quickly by the best of the Shinis' arrows, they fell like great trees broken by a mighty wind."}},{"n":9,"text":"रथैश्च बहुधा छिन्नैर्ध्वजैश्चैव विशां पते ।\nहयैश्च कनकापीडैः पतितैस्तत्र मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was covered with many cut chariots and banners, O lord of the people, and with fallen horses with golden trappings."}},{"n":10,"text":"शैनेयशरसंकृत्तैः शोणितौघपरिप्लुतैः ।\nअशोभत महाराज किंशुकैरिव पुष्पितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut by Shaineya's arrows and drenched in floods of blood, it shone, O great king, like flowering kimshuka trees."}},{"n":11,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः समरे युयुधानेन तावकाः ।\nत्रातारं नाध्यगच्छन्त पङ्कमग्ना इव द्विपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck in the battle by Yuyudhana, your men found no protector, like elephants stuck in mud."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्ते पर्यवर्तन्त सर्वे द्रोणरथं प्रति ।\nभयात्पतगराजस्य गर्तानीव महोरगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of them turned back toward Drona's chariot, as great serpents flee into holes for fear of the king of birds."}},{"n":13,"text":"हत्वा पञ्चशतान्योधाञ्शरैराशीविषोपमैः ।\nप्रायात्स शनकैर्वीरो धनंजयरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed five hundred warriors with arrows like venomous snakes, the hero went slowly on toward Dhananjaya's chariot."}},{"n":14,"text":"तं प्रयान्तं नरश्रेष्ठं पुत्रो दुःशासनस्तव ।\nविव्याध नवभिस्तूर्णं शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that best of men went on, your son Duhshasana quickly struck him with nine straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"स तु तं प्रतिविव्याध पञ्चभिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खैर्महेष्वासो गार्ध्रपत्रैरजिह्मगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty bowman struck him back with five sharp, straight, gold-feathered, vulture-fletched arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"सात्यकिं तु महाराज प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nदुःशासनस्त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा पुनर्विव्याध पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana, having struck Satyaki, O great king, with three arrows, as though laughing, struck him again with five."}},{"n":17,"text":"शैनेयस्तव पुत्रं तु विद्ध्वा पञ्चभिराशुगैः ।\nधनुश्चास्य रणे छित्त्वा विस्मयन्नर्जुनं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaineya, having pierced your son with five swift arrows and cut his bow in the battle, went on toward Arjuna, marveling."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो दुःशासनः क्रुद्धो वृष्णिवीराय गच्छते ।\nसर्वपारशवीं शक्तिं विससर्ज जिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duhshasana, enraged, hurled an all-iron spear at the Vrishni hero as he went, wishing to kill him."}},{"n":19,"text":"तां तु शक्तिं तदा घोरां तव पुत्रस्य सात्यकिः ।\nचिच्छेद शतधा राजन्निशितैः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Satyaki cut that terrible spear of your son into a hundred pieces with sharp heron-feathered arrows, O king."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय पुत्रस्तव जनेश्वर ।\nसात्यकिं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा सिंहनादं ननाद ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son, O lord of men, took another bow and, having struck Satyaki with ten arrows, roared a lion's roar."}},{"n":21,"text":"सात्यकिस्तु रणे क्रुद्धो मोहयित्वा सुतं तव ।\nशरैरग्निशिखाकारैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ।\nसर्वायसैस्तीक्ष्णवक्त्रैरष्टाभिर्विव्यधे पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Satyaki, enraged in the battle, having bewildered your son, struck him between the breasts with arrows like flames of fire, and again pierced him with eight all-iron, sharp-pointed arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"दुःशासनस्तु विंशत्या सात्यकिं प्रत्यविध्यत ।\nसात्वतोऽपि महाराज तं विव्याध स्तनान्तरे ।\nत्रिभिरेव महावेगैः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana struck Satyaki back with twenty, and the Satvata too, O great king, struck him between the breasts with three swift, straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततोऽस्य वाहान्निशितैः शरैर्जघ्ने महारथः ।\nसारथिं च सुसंक्रुद्धः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great chariot-warrior, in great anger, killed his horses with sharp arrows and his charioteer with straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"धनुरेकेन भल्लेन हस्तावापं च पञ्चभिः ।\nध्वजं च रथशक्तिं च भल्लाभ्यां परमास्त्रवित् ।\nचिच्छेद विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैस्तथोभौ पार्ष्णिसारथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The master of the best weapons cut his bow with one broad-headed arrow, his hand-guard with five, his banner and chariot-spear with two broad-headed arrows, and killed both his rear guard and his charioteer with sharp arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"स छिन्नधन्वा विरथो हताश्वो हतसारथिः ।\nत्रिगर्तसेनापतिना स्वरथेनापवाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His bow cut, chariotless, his horses and charioteer killed, he was carried off in his own chariot by the Trigarta commander."}},{"n":26,"text":"तमभिद्रुत्य शैनेयो मुहूर्तमिव भारत ।\nन जघान महाबाहुर्भीमसेनवचः स्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaineya, Bharata, pursued him and for a moment did not kill him, the mighty-armed one remembering Bhimasena's words."}},{"n":27,"text":"भीमसेनेन हि वधः सुतानां तव भारत ।\nप्रतिज्ञातः सभामध्ये सर्वेषामेव संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Bhimasena had pledged in the midst of the assembly that he would kill all your sons in battle."}},{"n":28,"text":"तथा दुःशासनं जित्वा सात्यकिः संयुगे प्रभो ।\nजगाम त्वरितो राजन्येन यातो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus beaten Duhshasana in battle, my lord, Satyaki went quickly, O king, where Dhananjaya had gone."}}]}]}